:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")
  DocsLinkGrid = import("/components/DocsLinkGrid.haml")
  DocsLinkCard = import("/components/DocsLinkCard.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Docs",
    title: "Plugin Reference",
    summary: "Built-in plugins cover Ruby, Haml, Markdown, CSS, JavaScript, assets, data imports, routing, and Google Fonts."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Default Plugin Set" }
    :markdown
      `Klenod::Build::Context.default_plugins` includes `RubyPlugin`, `IntlPlugin`, `HamlPlugin`, `MarkdownPlugin`, `CssPlugin`, `JavaScriptPlugin`, `SvgPlugin`, `ImagePlugin`, `JsonPlugin`, `YamlPlugin`, `TomlPlugin`, and `TextPlugin`.

      `RouterPlugin` and `GoogleFontsPlugin` are built in but opt-in. Applications can configure either one explicitly when they need routing or Google Fonts imports.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Hook Phases" }
    :markdown
      Plugins can implement:

      - `resolve(dependency, context)` to map an import specifier to a module id.
      - `load(module_id, context)` to provide source for virtual or custom modules.
      - `transform(module_id, code, context)` to rewrite source and record dependencies, assets, metadata, source maps, and watched patterns.
      - `finalize(module_id, result, resolved_dependencies, dependency_records, context)` to adjust a transform after eager dependency records are collected.
      - `import_value(resolved_dependency, record, context)` to provide development-time import values.
      - `runtime_import_value(resolved_dependency, record, context)` to provide serialized bundle import values.

      `resolve`, `load`, `transform`, and `finalize` are collection-time hooks. They must not depend on evaluated app exports. `runtime_import_value` must return serializable values or runtime instructions.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Core Plugins" }
    %DocsLinkGrid
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/RubyPlugin"),
        title: "RubyPlugin",
        summary: "Ruby modules, import rewriting, lazy imports, glob imports, and runtime import values."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/HamlPlugin"),
        title: "HamlPlugin",
        summary: "Haml components, companion CSS, intl files, source maps, filters, and component tags."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/MarkdownPlugin"),
        title: "MarkdownPlugin",
        summary: "Markdown files and Haml markdown filters rendered through application components."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/CssPlugin"),
        title: "CssPlugin",
        summary: "Scoped CSS, stylesheet assets, CSS imports, class maps, and URL dependencies."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/JavascriptPlugin"),
        title: "JavaScriptPlugin",
        summary: "JavaScript, TypeScript, TSX custom elements, CSS module imports, asset metadata imports, source maps, and minification."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/Assets"),
        title: "Asset Plugins",
        summary: "SVG and raster image imports with content types, dimensions, variants, and generated files."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/DataPlugins"),
        title: "Data Plugins",
        summary: "JSON, YAML, TOML, and text modules imported as Ruby values."
      }
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/IntlPlugin"),
        title: "IntlPlugin",
        summary: "Translation companions for Haml modules."
      }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Opt-In Plugins" }
    %DocsLinkGrid
      %DocsLinkCard{
        href: localized_path("/docs/plugins/RouterPlugin"),
